@startuml plugin-kernel
' Render with: plantuml -tpng docs/Design/SoftArchitecture/figures/plugin-kernel.puml
!include style.iuml
set separator none
title Plug-in kernel: a module plugs in, the kernel never changes

class "main.py" as main <<kernel>> {
  ~ create_app(plugins = PLUGINS): FastAPI
}
class "registry.py" as registry <<kernel>> {
  ~ PLUGINS: tuple[Plugin, ...]
}

package "Modules" as modules {
  class "users/plugin.py" as users <<entry point>> {
    + PLUGIN: Plugin
    .. its values ..
    name = "users"
    no routes yet
  }
  class "wallet/plugin.py" as wallet <<entry point>> {
    + PLUGIN: Plugin
    .. its values ..
    name = "wallet"
    router = routes.router
  }
  class "market/plugin.py" as market <<entry point>> {
    + PLUGIN: Plugin
    .. its values ..
    name = "market"
    router = routes.router
    lifespan = poller.lifespan
    health = poller.health
  }
  class "trading/plugin.py" as trading <<entry point>> {
    + PLUGIN: Plugin
    .. its values ..
    name = "trading"
    router = routes.router
  }
  class "activity/plugin.py (#190)" as activity <<not built yet>>
}

package "app/core/plugins.py" as core {
  class Plugin <<data>> {
    + name: str
    + router: APIRouter or None
    + lifespan: Lifespan or None
    + health: HealthCheck or None
    .. it refuses ..
    a lifespan without a health check
  }
}

main --> registry : reads
registry --> users
registry --> wallet
registry --> market : lists
registry --> trading
registry ..> activity : later
users --> Plugin
wallet --> Plugin
market --> Plugin
trading --> Plugin

note right of main
  Adds each router under /v1, starts each
  lifespan in order and stops them in reverse,
  and shows each health check in GET /v1/health.
end note

legend right
  <color:#5F5E5A>■</color> Kernel
  <color:#854F0B>■</color> A module's plugin
  <color:#185FA5>■</color> Data: a record
  <color:#B4B2A9>□</color> Not built yet
  + code outside its own module may use it
  ~ only the kernel's files may use it
  An arrow means "uses".
  To add a module: write its plugin.py,
  add one line to PLUGINS, and add it
  to the layers in pyproject.toml.
endlegend
@enduml
